{
  "description": "An Apply EDL node before and after the person picks an OLDER take in the config-panel results gallery (`cases`), and before and after a workflow run lands a new take on it (`runs`). `after` is exactly what the editor saves: the frontend tests click the real gallery (frontend/src/components/editor/config-panels/__tests__/apply-edl-picked-take.test.tsx) or run the real run-result lane (frontend/src/components/editor/workflow-editor/__tests__/sync-node-states-named-outputs.test.ts) and require the result to equal `after`; the server test (apply-edl-picked-take.test.ts, beside this folder) runs the orchestrator's saved-data path on `after`. Both require the selected take, generatedResults[activeResultIndex], to be what a downstream node receives, as the medium it is, with the Transcript that take was cut with, or with no Transcript at all when the editor cannot know that take's (never another take's). A case with a `job` is a take with no Transcript of its own: the editor reads it back from that job (GET /v1/jobs/:id/status, as the API returns it). Every lane that lands a run's take writes the Transcript that render was cut with, on the node and on the take, or clears the node's when it was cut with none (`runs.video`, `runs.untranscribed`).",
